From a04612e9c7d07282d8fc817d52072f849564ce9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:31:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-2: jump to the DFM definition, trace a button's
 command into the C++ server, show where the form code uses a control (0.2.0)

- DFM: the control's "object Name: TClass" line in the BCB6 .dfm, and every
  property's own line (double-click a property -> that line), read-only Big5
- web -> C++: follow the handler into what it calls (depth 3, same-file
  definitions first) to cmd()/rawCmd()/raw()/run(); then the server's dispatch
  branch (== "x.y", case, strcmp, command table) and the function it hands the
  command to (same-line call only -- a block dispatch IS the handler)
- uses: "spbSave->..." and the declaration, only in files that implement or
  declare the form class
- find component: Ctrl+Alt+O quick pick over every control of the page
- fix: CRLF C++ files -- "#endif\r" never matched, so an "#if 0" never closed
  (wb_serve.cpp was dead from line 3322 on); the old csystem.cpp test passed
  only because it counted the forward declaration

Tests: lib 49 / probe 2 pages / fake vscode 30 / real VS Code 29 + 8-page
sweep -- all pass, opened files byte-identical (MD5) before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
